---
title: Exif reader
tags: tools
summary: >-
    Reads the metadata stored in images, such as GPS position and camera details, where puzzle makers often hide information.
noLimits: true
---
{% from "macros/tool.njk" import toolSection with context %}
{% from "macros/tool-frame.njk" import fileFrame %}
{% set filename = page.fileSlug %}
{% set intro %}
    <p>That includes GPS information, and camera information such as the exposure, the aperture, and the device's make and model, from a variety of image file types.</p>
    <p>Text fields, such as comments and descriptions, are shown first, and any value that looks encoded (as binary, hex or Base64) is marked, with a link that opens it in <a href="/convrtrs/" class="text-convrtr" data-convrtrs-link>Convrtrs</a> to decode. Every tag follows, grouped by where it's stored in the file.</p>
    <p>Supports <code class="tool-example">JPEG</code> <code class="tool-example">TIFF</code> <code class="tool-example">PNG</code> <code class="tool-example">HEIC</code> <code class="tool-example">AVIF</code> <code class="tool-example">WebP</code> <code class="tool-example">GIF</code></p>
    <p class="tool-about__credit">Powered by <a href="https://github.com/mattiasw/ExifReader" class="text-convrtr">ExifReader</a> by Mattias Wallander, under the <a href="https://mozilla.org/MPL/2.0/" class="text-convrtr">Mozilla Public License 2.0</a>.</p>
{% endset %}
